/* The header for this test is at the BOTTOM of this file, below the script.
   It is there because a constant inside a leading comment can swallow the
   rest of the file in the engine - see RMSTEST_56 and the directory README.
   Nothing below the script can do any harm. */

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

  create_land
  {
    terrain_type GRASS2
    base_size 3
    number_of_tiles 150
    zone 2
    land_position 15 50
  }
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type GRASS2
    base_size 3
    number_of_tiles 150
    zone 3
    land_position 85 50
  }

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<TERRAIN_GENERATION>


<OBJECTS_GENERATION>


<CONNECTION_GENERATION>

  create_connect_all_lands
  {
    replace_terrain GRASS ROAD
  }

/*
================================================================================
RMSTEST_77b - control/twin for RMSTEST_77a. Identical map, identical
command, with the "terrain_size GRASS 1 0" line removed entirely so the
path is painted under whatever the engine's OWN undeclared default is,
rather than the value this project assumes that default equals.
Feeds: docs/preview-design.md Sec.6.5, same item as 77a.

Byte-for-byte the same two lands, same positions, same zones as 77a. The
only difference is the missing terrain_size line - GRASS is still declared
replaceable, so a path still paints ROAD, just under whatever radius and
variance the engine applies when the script itself says nothing.

READING THE PAIR TOGETHER
  77a and 77b MATCH (both clean, one patch each; or both fragmented the
    same way) -> the assumed default (radius 1, variance 0) is confirmed,
    since declaring it explicitly changes nothing.
  77a is CLEAN and 77b is FRAGMENTED -> the undeclared default carries
    real variance greater than 0 that an explicit "1 0" declaration does
    not reproduce. Sec.6.5's doc-stated default is wrong and needs a
    measured variance value in its place - re-run 77b at increasing
    declared variance (1, 2, 3...) until the fragmentation rate matches,
    which pins the true constant.
  77a is ALSO fragmented -> see 77a's own header; the fragmentation isn't
    about terrain_size's variance at all, and this pair has ruled out the
    hypothesis it was built to test rather than confirmed it.

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200), ANY PLAYER COUNT. THREE RUNS, matching 77a.

READ WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --patches ROAD
  Same read as 77a: patch count, area, circularity. Put the two result
  tables side by side before concluding anything.
================================================================================
*/
